    "title": "Split a Binary Search Tree by a Key",
    "category": "Binary Search Trees",
    "difficulty": "Hard",
    "problemStatement": "Given the root of a Binary Search Tree and a key X, split the tree into two Binary Search Trees such that one contains all keys less than or equal to X and the other contains all keys greater than X.",
